\label{proposition_abstract_1}
{\rm (1)} $A$ is $H$-smooth with bound $a$ if and only if,  for any $\psi\in {\mathcal{H}}$, $e^{-itH}\psi$ belongs to $D(A)$ for a.e. $t\in {\mathbb{R}}$ and 
\begin{align}
\label{proposition_abstract_1_1}
\norm{Ae^{-itH}\psi}_{L^2({\mathbb{R}};{\mathcal{H}})}
