\end{align}
{\rm (2)} Suppose $A$ is $H$-supersmooth with bound $a$. Then, for any simple function $F:{\mathbb{R}}\to D(A^*)$ and $t\in {\mathbb{R}}$, $Ae^{-i(t-s)H}A^*F(s)$ is Bochner integrable in $s$ over $[0,t]$ (or $[t,0]$) and satisfies 
\begin{align}
\label{proposition_abstract_1_2}
\bignorm{e^{-|{\varepsilon} t|}\int_0^t Ae^{-i(t-s)H}A^*F(s)ds}_{L^2({\mathbb{R}};{\mathcal{H}})}\le a\norm{e^{-|{\varepsilon} t|}F}_{L^2({\mathbb{R}};{\mathcal{H}})}
\end{align}
for all ${\varepsilon}\in {\mathbb{R}}$. Conversely, if the estimate \eqref{proposition_abstract_1_2}  holds for all simple function $F:{\mathbb{R}}\to D(A^*)$ and $|{\varepsilon}|<{\varepsilon}_0$ with some ${\varepsilon}_0>0$, then $A$ is $H$-supersmooth with bound $a$.

Let $\Gamma_H$ be the inhomogeneous propagator defined by the formula \eqref{inhomogeneous_propagator} and set
